    "investigated_but_blocked": [
      "No city in this batch was left with zero record, but mid.org and cityoftracy.org refused automated connections outright (ECONNREFUSED), while cityofmerced.gov, clovisca.gov, tulare.ca.gov, and manteca.gov all returned HTTP 403 on every attempt — these five records are correspondingly thinner, built from search-engine-indexed page titles/URLs with reduced confidence."
    ],
    "recurring_source_access_problems": [
      "Multiple installer/SEO marketing sites (northvalleysolarpower and similar domains) dominated early search results for Tracy specifically, offering a specific 'SolarAPP+ enabled, ~1 week' claim; per the source policy against using installer/SEO sites as evidence, none of this content was used, and the Tracy record instead relies only on the city's own (blocked) page title and a general inspection-scheduling contact number found via search indexing."
    ],
    "schema_gaps_discovered": [
      "No new schema gaps were discovered while collecting this batch."
    ],
    "trust_rule_corrections_made_during_collection": [
      "This batch surfaced a third and fourth distinct municipal electric utility beyond SMUD and Roseville Electric: Modesto Irrigation District (MID) and Turlock Irrigation District (TID), both irrigation districts that also operate as vertically-integrated electric utilities, plus a fifth, Lodi Electric Utility (LEU). Each required an individual verification step rather than assuming PG&E coverage by default for these Central Valley cities.",
      "Visalia and Tulare (city) required recognizing that SCE's service territory extends into parts of Tulare County in the Central Valley, not just Southern California — a genuine exception to the otherwise PG&E-dominated Central Valley pattern, confirmed via multiple corroborating sources (a chamber-of-commerce utility listing for Visalia, and SCE's own incorporated-cities fact sheet for Tulare).",
      "Tulare County's own SolarAPP+ program (tularecounty.ca.gov) was found to apply explicitly only to unincorporated county areas, not incorporated cities like Tulare or Visalia — this distinction was caught and the county program was not used as a substitute source for either city record."
    ]
